  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Atfaluna Society for Deaf Children</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Act 1.1.1 Coordinate distribution of Adolescent Girl Humanitarian Package to adolescent girls in different locations and IDP shelters.
Atfaluna works with 4 Women Led Organizations (Al-A&#x2019;wdah, Beit Al-Mustaqbal, Womens Programs Centre and Shafi Association of Jabalia) and will reach 1230  young adolescent girls in these different WLO centres and UNRWA schools in Middle (Deir Al-Balah) and Southern (Rafah) governorates of Gaza.

Act 1.1.2 Awareness raising and recreational activities for adolescent girls tailored to their specific protection concerns and their wellbeing
Once the ceasefire is reached and conditions safe, all partners, including Atfaluna, will be able to carry out the activities in a structured way, targeting three groups of girls (20 to 25 girls) per week and each group will receive one awareness and one recreational session.

Act 1.2.1 Coordinate distribution of supplements and other nutrition supplements to pregnant and lactating women and adolescent girls in different locations and IDP shelters
Initially Atfalouna estimates to be able to distribute to 847 supplements and nutrition items to women in middle and Southern Gaza (Rafah and Deir Al Balah) and girls and is regularly assessing the needs, expecting the number to severely increase.

Act 1.2.2 Conduct awareness sessions to pregnant and lactating women and adolescent girls and information sharing via women&#x2019;s networks
Atfaluna, in coordination with 7 CSO/WRO in the community, will continue its case management referral system operationalization and will provide community awareness for pregnant and lactating women and girls.

Act 1.2.3 Establish women and adolescent girls maternal spaces for breastfeeding practices
Once the ceasefire is reached and conditions safe, all partners will review working modality which will require revision of the activity and budget.

Act 1.3.1 Conduct assessments in &#x2018;hot spot&#x2019; locations (hospitals, shelters, etc.) to identify, register (using UNICEF Platform) and refer cases of Unaccompanied and Separated Children
Oxfam and child protection partners (Wefaq, Atfaluna, AISHA) will define and update ways of working in close coordination with UNICEF and the CP AoR, based on criteria and referral pathways shared.</narrative>
  </description>
